{"id": "EUVD-2026-103959", "enisaUuid": "11546d0c-976d-3c8d-9abc-6798beaa1eba", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: account proxy paths against the mesh path limit\n\nProxy-path churn can drive the interface path counter negative and let\nlater mesh path additions exceed MESH_MAX_MPATHS.\n\nmesh_path_free_rcu() decrements the interface mpaths counter for entries\nfrom both the mesh and proxy path tables, but mpp_path_add() never\nreserves a slot in that counter. Removing or expiring a proxy path\ntherefore returns a slot that was never charged.\n\nmesh_path_add() uses the same counter to enforce MESH_MAX_MPATHS, so once\nit falls below the number of installed paths the limit no longer holds.\n\nReserve the shared quota before allocating a proxy path and release it on\nevery unsuccessful addition. Mesh and proxy paths now share one\n1024-entry budget, so mpp_path_add() can return -ENOSPC at that limit.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:46:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:53", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c66ab4b94bb04c162485759196555e08c0965320", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/df072db65fdaa34ad15e1d66fc06a53e3e97f778", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3b75831ceee76d32bb8e7ddd241904f92f9b5407", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5a32409ed34a1868830899a5d2437f0b3bf3532c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a5f35d4b112af1415ff06bd501c8cc26cc08aa8b"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r63c-mg4x-3hrx", "CVE-2026-98705"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "264f22d8-254c-36c2-b6b7-abbeac0e1e03", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ece1a2e7e86078c8379937b546e32cb7f25fcb6c <a5f35d4b112af1415ff06bd501c8cc26cc08aa8b"}, {"id": "34cbc49b-983e-314a-b6ec-795aa4b4eb2d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3f4caa8c-411e-39ea-b09f-f88b14a58abb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ece1a2e7e86078c8379937b546e32cb7f25fcb6c <3b75831ceee76d32bb8e7ddd241904f92f9b5407"}, {"id": "432ffe0e-7f2a-3b7d-8cfe-a8124c366dfa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4740ea68-3351-35fd-bfd3-6aa97902e01b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "80b7c22f-a792-38c2-b2fc-6a36051e21ec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ece1a2e7e86078c8379937b546e32cb7f25fcb6c <c66ab4b94bb04c162485759196555e08c0965320"}, {"id": "8d2998d6-c15b-3d34-bb4b-799243dfb7af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "d555ddc2-37e4-3724-8746-218053670473", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "d90d7898-8dfd-3c4e-9d95-cebdd195f23b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "e23588c4-752f-3a2b-b759-3958a9c3ff62", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ece1a2e7e86078c8379937b546e32cb7f25fcb6c <df072db65fdaa34ad15e1d66fc06a53e3e97f778"}, {"id": "f41acfed-212e-345e-9a46-d85876d30e9a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.2"}, {"id": "fa09dd4e-6e3f-32d5-9b3c-77dbd6e93cb9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ece1a2e7e86078c8379937b546e32cb7f25fcb6c <5a32409ed34a1868830899a5d2437f0b3bf3532c"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6f100c06-f5ba-3b55-9279-656ed11630de", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}